% CONFORM ERROR -- the IF1 ERROR channel, exercised on the failing path.
%
% The frontend has always built a full apparatus for a non-conforming
% elementwise operation: a per-element compatibility flag, an AND-fold of it,
% and a NOT giving "this did not conform", handed to an ERROR node on a separate
% `::` channel that ends at a PANIC boundary.  All of it survived into the
% emitted C -- and then the ERROR node lowered to a CONSTANT, so the verdict was
% computed and thrown away.  `a + b` with mismatched extents silently
% zero-padded to the longer operand:
%
%     5 + 3  ->  [ 11 22 33 4 5 ]      b's missing tail read as 0
%     3 + 5  ->  [ 11 22 33 40 50 ]    result grew to b's length
%
% Nothing covered that, because every group fed conforming inputs -- including
% dv_agreement, the group named for this ("Error Monad" in positive.t), whose
% driver only ever passed two length-3 arrays.
%
% This program exists to be run BOTH ways: its harness calls it once with equal
% extents (which must compute) and once with unequal ones in a forked child
% (which must abort).  A test that only ever takes the passing branch is what
% let the gap survive.

define main

type Ints = array_dv[integer];

function main( a, b : Ints returns Ints )
  a + b
end function
